#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059395 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf8cae61-212a-5005-8aa8-b34fce63523f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Metric Units of Length"}] :question/id #uuid "d12c87c0-6317-5546-9a7c-145b35a5b741" :question/math-academy-id "e-12508" :question/problem "Suppose we want to measure the length of the Golden Gate Bridge (California, USA). Which of the following metric units could we use?\n\nI. $\\rm{s}$\n\nII. $\\rm{kg}$\n\nIII. $\\rm{km}$" :question/worked-solution "A table showing the metric units of length is given below.\n\n| Name | Symbol |\n| --- | --- |\n| Kilometer | $\\textrm{km}$ |\n| Meter | $\\textrm{m}$ |\n| Centimeter | $\\textrm{cm}$ |\n| Millimeter | $\\textrm{mm}$ |\n\nTherefore, from the given options, the only unit of length is $\\textrm{km}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059396 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e0d75fe-4f9a-51ba-bcd6-9d85a26e6eac" :knowledge-point/title "Stating Length Conversions in Metric Units"}] :question/id #uuid "61f7fc3b-b519-53d7-955d-1619221c67b7" :question/math-academy-id "e-12509" :question/problem "A window is $1 \\, \\textrm{m}$ wide. What is this length in centimeters?" :question/worked-solution "A table showing the metric units of length is given below.\n\n| Name | Symbol | Conversion |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Kilometer | $\\textrm{km}$ | $1\\,\\textrm{km} = 1\\,000\\,\\textrm{m}$ |\n| Meter | $\\textrm{m}$ | Base Unit |\n| Centimeter | $\\textrm{cm}$ | $100\\,\\textrm{cm} = 1\\,\\textrm{m}$ |\n| Millimeter | $\\textrm{mm}$ | $1\\,000\\,\\textrm{mm} = 1\\,\\textrm{m}$ |\n\nSo, $1 \\, \\textrm{m}$ is equivalent to $100 \\, \\textrm{cm}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059397 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059838 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b97b513f-cac2-5c03-9a79-93e1797392c7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Customary Units of Length"}] :